# Design artifacts must round-trip BYTE-IDENTICAL.
#
# ASCII STL looks like text to git, so without this it "helpfully" rewrites CRLF->LF on
# checkout. The mesh stays valid, but the bytes change -- which silently breaks every
# md5/size check used to prove a printable matches the model it was verified against.
# The .3mf files are ZIP archives; a single mangled byte makes them unopenable.
*.stl   -text
*.3mf   binary
*.gcode -text
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.pdf   binary

# .scad is the authored source -- normal text, diff it.
